# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown

# DHCP client finite-state machine (RFC 2131 §4.4, simplified).
# Interim: block. Planned: statechart genre.
#
# MULTI-LINE guide/authoring.md DEMO:
#   1) node labels:  "NAME\nshort role"     → wraps on canvas
#   2) edge mids:    -["why\nwhat"]->         → reason always on the drawing
#   3) # blocks:     multi-line prose         → edit like Markdown (not in SVG)
#   4) table cells:  text<br>more             → multi-line list form
#
# Why some paths used to look "unlabeled": SVG only shows mid labels, not
# # comments. Every edge mid is now two lines: reason + action/outcome.
figdown 0.1 block
title "DHCP client statechart (RFC 2131)\nmulti-line authoring sample"

class mode "DHCP client protocol state" fill=#e0e7ff

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# STATES — multi-line canvas label + multi-line # narrative
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

node init "INIT\nno lease" class=mode
# No usable IPv4 lease on the interface.
# Next step is usually broadcast DISCOVER, unless a stored lease
# steers the client into INIT-REBOOT instead.

node selecting "SELECTING\ncollect OFFERs" class=mode
# One or more DHCPOFFER frames have arrived.
# Client has not yet committed to a server / address.

node requesting "REQUESTING\nawait ACK/NAK" class=mode
# DHCPREQUEST outstanding (selecting an OFFER, or confirming
# a remembered address on the reboot path).

node bound "BOUND\nlease active" class=mode
# Address in use (yiaddr / assigned).
# T1 and T2 timers run; data plane may use the lease.

node renewing "RENEWING\nT1 unicast" class=mode
# T1 fired. Client unicasts DHCPREQUEST to the server
# that granted the current lease.

node rebinding "REBINDING\nT2 broadcast" class=mode
# T2 fired (or renew path gave up). Client broadcasts
# DHCPREQUEST so any server may extend the lease.

node init_reboot "INIT-REBOOT\nstored lease" class=mode
# Power-on (or restart) with a previously allocated address
# still believed valid; confirm before using it.

node rebooting "REBOOTING\nconfirm lease" class=mode
# Confirmation REQUEST in flight for the remembered address.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TRANSITIONS — every mid is reason + outcome (visible on SVG)
# # comments hold longer prose for .fd editors (not drawn)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# --- acquire ---
edge init -["need address\nsnd DISCOVER"]-> selecting
# trigger: begin acquire (no stored lease, or policy chooses discover)
# effect:  broadcast DHCPDISCOVER; start collecting DHCPOFFER

edge selecting -["offer chosen\nsnd REQUEST"]-> requesting
# trigger: client picks one OFFER
# effect:  broadcast DHCPREQUEST with server-id + requested-ip

edge requesting -["server grants\nACK → use IP"]-> bound
# trigger: DHCPACK
# effect:  install address; arm T1/T2; interface up for that lease

edge requesting -["REQUEST failed\nNAK/timeout → INIT"]-> init
# trigger: DHCPNAK, or retries exhausted
# effect:  discard candidate; return to INIT
# note:    individual REQUEST retransmits are collapsed (not drawn)

# --- renew / rebind ---
edge bound -["T1: renew time\nunicast REQUEST"]-> renewing
# trigger: T1 (renewal time)
# effect:  unicast DHCPREQUEST to binding server

edge renewing -["lease extended\nACK → BOUND"]-> bound
# trigger: DHCPACK from binding server
# effect:  refresh lease timers; stay configured

edge renewing -["server refuses\nNAK → drop IP"]-> init
# trigger: DHCPNAK
# effect:  stop using address; rediscover

edge renewing -["T2: rebind time\nbcast REQUEST"]-> rebinding
# trigger: T2 (rebinding time) while still unacked
# effect:  broaden REQUEST to broadcast

edge rebinding -["any server OK\nACK → BOUND"]-> bound
# trigger: DHCPACK from any willing server
# effect:  new binding parameters; back to BOUND

edge rebinding -["no lease left\nNAK / expiry"]-> init
# trigger: DHCPNAK, or lease lifetime ends
# effect:  must not use address; INIT

# --- reboot path ---
edge init -["remembered lease\n→ confirm path"]-> init_reboot
# trigger: non-volatile lease remembered across restart
# else:    remain INIT and take DISCOVER path

edge init_reboot -["confirm stored lease\nsnd REQUEST (bcast)"]-> rebooting
# trigger: start confirmation of remembered address
# effect:  broadcast DHCPREQUEST for that address
# (this is the INIT-REBOOT → REBOOTING arc — pinned on its own row below)

edge rebooting -["lease confirmed\nACK → BOUND"]-> bound
# trigger: server confirms stored address
# effect:  configure interface; arm timers (same as acquire ACK)

edge rebooting -["cannot confirm\nNAK/timeout → INIT"]-> init
# trigger: refusal or no answer
# effect:  forget stored lease; full rediscover

# --- release / loss ---
edge bound -["give up / lost lease\nRELEASE → INIT"]-> init
# trigger: DHCPRELEASE, or lease lost without renew
# effect:  optional DHCPRELEASE; clear configuration

# Hand layout: three bands — the cold-acquire row, the reboot row beneath
# it, and the renew/rebind column under BOUND. Presentation only (`GUI-WRITEBACK-STRUCTURE`):
# delete every `pin` below and all eight states and all fifteen labelled
# transitions are still here, in the `node`/`edge` lines above.
#
# RE-AUTHORED (`EDGE-GEOMETRY-CONSTRUCTS`), AND THIS FIGURE IS WHY THE MEASUREMENT
# MATTERED. It used to open the zone with `routing orthogonal` and carry
# five hand-routed lines that ran short return corridors just under
# the acquire row. All six constructs were WITHDRAWN from the language —
# see spec/migrations.md 0.1 and core §9 `EDGE-IDENTITY-AND-GEOMETRY` — and the geometry
# they encoded had SHIPPED A DEFECT: the corridors reached x=20 and the
# canvas only ever grew right and down, so the published artifact drew
# "membered lease" for "remembered lease" and "nnot confirm" for "cannot
# confirm". Author waypoints did not protect this figure; they clipped it.
#
# The grid below is the same three bands, opened out. The old one was
# built for corridors — 140 px between centres, boxes 96-112 px wide —
# so with the corridors gone the transition labels printed straight over
# the node boxes. Centres are now ~220 px apart and the reboot row sits
# 220 px down, which is the whole fix: no clipping, no label over a box.
# On tools/layout-lint.js the figure went 23 -> 8 (the tightest possible
# strip scores 6, but it is the one that overprints labels, which the
# linter does not measure — the number was checked against the picture,
# not instead of it).
flow right
layout
# row 0 — cold acquire, left to right
pin init at=(20,40) width=96 height=44
pin selecting at=(230,40) width=112 height=44
pin requesting at=(450,40) width=112 height=44
pin bound at=(670,40) width=100 height=44
# row 1 left — reboot path under INIT/SELECTING
pin init_reboot at=(20,260) width=112 height=44
pin rebooting at=(230,260) width=112 height=44
# column under BOUND — renew then rebind
pin renewing at=(670,160) width=100 height=44
pin rebinding at=(666,280) width=108 height=44

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# COMPANION TABLES — multi-line cells via <br>
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

figdown 0.1 table
table states "State catalog (multi-line notes in cells)"
| State       | Role on wire                         | What the client is waiting for      |
|-------------|--------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|
| INIT        | no lease                             | policy to DISCOVER<br>or INIT-REBOOT |
| SELECTING   | OFFERs arriving                      | choose server / address             |
| REQUESTING  | REQUEST outstanding                  | ACK or NAK                          |
| BOUND       | address configured<br>T1/T2 running  | T1, RELEASE, or link loss           |
| RENEWING    | unicast renew                        | ACK, NAK, or T2                     |
| REBINDING   | broadcast renew                      | ACK, NAK, or lease end              |
| INIT-REBOOT | remembered lease                     | send confirm REQUEST                |
| REBOOTING   | confirm REQUEST out                  | ACK or NAK/timeout                  |

figdown 0.1 table
table tr "Transition list (why → what)"
| From → To              | Why (reason)                    | What happens                            |
|------------------------|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| INIT → SELECTING       | need an address                 | snd DHCPDISCOVER (bcast)                |
| SELECTING → REQUESTING | an OFFER was chosen             | snd DHCPREQUEST (bcast)                 |
| REQUESTING → BOUND     | server grants lease             | configure if;<br>arm T1/T2                |
| REQUESTING → INIT      | refused or timed out            | discard candidate;<br>restart             |
| BOUND → RENEWING       | T1 renewal time                 | unicast REQUEST                         |
| RENEWING → BOUND       | lease extended                  | reset timers                            |
| RENEWING → INIT        | server refuses                  | drop address                            |
| RENEWING → REBINDING   | T2; binding server silent       | broadcast REQUEST                       |
| REBINDING → BOUND      | some server extends             | accept new binding                      |
| REBINDING → INIT       | no lease left                   | stop using address                      |
| INIT → INIT-REBOOT     | remembered lease at boot        | skip cold DISCOVER                      |
| INIT-REBOOT → REBOOTING| must confirm old IP             | bcast REQUEST for old addr              |
| REBOOTING → BOUND      | lease confirmed                 | same as acquire ACK                     |
| REBOOTING → INIT       | cannot confirm                  | full rediscover                         |
| BOUND → INIT           | release or lease lost           | optional DHCPRELEASE;<br>clear config     |
